@startuml OperatorName
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: how `proveo init` asks the operator's name once and every agent's house rules address them by it, with "Executor" as the default
' covers: internal/operator/operator.go
' covers: internal/operator/operator_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/init_operator.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/init_operator_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/init.go (operatorStage after credentialStage)
' covers: internal/run/run.go (operator.Env on both backends)
' covers: internal/ui/ui.go (SectionOperator)
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh (_proveo_operator_name, _proveo_address_operator, proveo_compose_house_rules, proveo_address_operator_claude)
' covers: internal/contract/operator_name_test.go
' covers: e2e/operator_name_test.go
' covers: defs/claudecode/mcp/Dockerfile (/etc/claude-code/CLAUDE.md owned by the agent user)
'   the plan item this delivers ......... _spec/_plans/white-label-brand-manifest.puml (D)
'   the init stages around it ........... _spec/cmd/proveo/init-credential-entry.puml
'
' ── WHY ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' The images bake this repository's AGENTS.md as proveo's house rules
' (/opt/proveo/AGENTS.md for every harness, /etc/claude-code/CLAUDE.md for
' claudecode), and its first rule reads `Address me as "Executor"`. That made
' one maintainer's preference every operator's name. The template keeps the
' line; each host now decides the name.
'
' ── ASK (proveo init, last stage) ──────────────────────────────────────────
'   form     title "Greetings, how may I address you?", one field `name`,
'            placeholder = the stored name, else Executor
'   keep     operator.Sanitize: first 16 runes, trimmed, no quotes, backslashes,
'            backticks or control characters
'   empty    keeps the stored name; with none stored, Executor and no file
'   skipped  --print, --yes or no terminal: reports the name in use
'   store    ~/.proveo/operator.yml   `name: <value>`  (PROVEO_HOME honoured)
'
' ── CARRY (proveo run) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   sbx      agent env PROVEO_OPERATOR_NAME=<name>
'   docker   -e PROVEO_OPERATOR_NAME, value on the docker process (ChildEnv)
'   none     nothing is passed when no name is stored
'
' ── APPLY (the seed, before the agent is released) ─────────────────────────
'   _proveo_operator_name     re-sanitizes; 16 characters under C.UTF-8, so a
'                             multibyte name is cut by character, not byte
'   _proveo_address_operator  rewrites every `Address me as "…"` on stdin;
'                             awk reads the name from ENVIRON with & escaped,
'                             so no character can reach the pattern syntax
'   codex, opencode           proveo_compose_house_rules filters the template
'                             into the user-level instructions block
'   claudecode                proveo_address_operator_claude rewrites the
'                             managed /etc/claude-code/CLAUDE.md in place (the
'                             image hands that file to the agent user)
'   no name                   every file stays as baked: "Executor"
' The /opt/proveo/AGENTS.md template is never edited, so every run starts from
' the shipped default and a removed name takes effect on the next boot.

actor "Operator" as OP
node "host" as HOST {
  component "proveo init\noperator stage" as INIT
  component "~/.proveo/operator.yml\nname: <16 runes>" as FILE <<db>>
  component "proveo run" as RUN
}
node "sandbox" as VM {
  component "seed\n_proveo_address_operator" as SEED
  component "house rules\nAddress me as \"<name>\"" as RULES
}

OP --> INIT : "Greetings, how may I address you?"
INIT --> FILE : Sanitize + Save
RUN --> FILE : operator.Env
RUN --> SEED : PROVEO_OPERATOR_NAME
SEED --> RULES : codex/opencode block,\nclaudecode managed CLAUDE.md

note right of FILE
  **Empty keeps, nothing defaults.** A blank
  answer keeps a stored name; with none stored
  no file is written and agents keep calling
  the operator Executor.
end note

note right of SEED
  **The name cannot escape its quotes.** Host
  and seed both drop quotes, backslashes and
  control characters; awk takes it from the
  environment with & escaped.
end note
@enduml
